gMH(){return"The day master's own element and polarity \u2014 an equal. It reads as siblings, peers and rivals of one's own rank, and as self-reliance. It supports a weak day master and crowds a strong one."},
gMX(){return"The same element, opposite polarity \u2014 a peer who competes rather than assists. It shares the day master's strength and its wealth, so it reads as partnership and as rivalry in the same breath."},
gMP(){return"What the day master produces, same polarity \u2014 expression that flows without strain. Traditionally the star of appetite, craft and contentment: talent given out easily."},
gMR(){return"What the day master produces, opposite polarity \u2014 expression with an edge. Brilliant and unruly; it makes performers and critics, and it wears against the Direct Officer, which is authority."},
gMV(){return"What the day master controls, same polarity \u2014 wealth arriving irregularly. Opportunity, enterprise and windfall rather than salary; traditionally also the father, and an open hand with money."},
gMN(){return"What the day master controls, opposite polarity \u2014 wealth held steadily. Salary, property and careful management. In a man's chart it traditionally stands for the wife as well."},
gMZ(){return"What controls the day master, same polarity \u2014 pressure with no cushion. Force, risk and decisive action: well handled it is courage, badly handled it is being driven."},
gMJ(){return"What controls the day master, opposite polarity \u2014 authority one accepts. Office, rules, reputation and duty. In a woman's chart it traditionally stands for the husband as well."},
gMT(){return"What produces the day master, same polarity \u2014 support given unevenly. Intuition, unusual learning and a mind that goes its own way; traditionally it can also starve the Eating God."},
gML(){return"What produces the day master, opposite polarity \u2014 support given steadily. Education, protection and backing; traditionally the mother. It strengthens the day master and softens the pressure on it."},
gNR(){return"Peach Blossom"},
gNO(){return"Nobleman"},
gNU(){return"Travelling Horse"},
gNF(){return"Academic"},
gNI(){return"Canopy"},
gNL(){return"General"},
gNT(){return"Romance and charm"},
gNQ(){return"Help and protection"},
gNW(){return"Travel and movement"},
gNH(){return"Study and writing"},
gNK(){return"Art and solitude"},
gNN(){return"Authority and command"},
gNS(){return"The flower of attraction \u2014 charm, romance and the notice of others. It is read from the day branch's trine, and the branch it names is where that charm attaches. Absent, attraction is simply not one of the chart's defining threads."},
gNP(){return"The helper who arrives when needed: mentors, patrons, the door that opens at the right moment. It is the one star read from a pair of branches rather than from one. Where it falls is where support tends to come from."},
gNV(){return"The post horse \u2014 journeys, relocation, and a restlessness that will not sit still. It faces the opening of the day branch's trine, so it marks movement outward. In the year pillar it reads as distance from where one began; in the hour, as movement late in life."},
gNG(){return"The star of study, writing and examinations. Read from the day stem, it points at the branch where learning comes easily. Its presence favours scholarship and clear expression rather than luck."},
gNJ(){return"The canopy over the carriage: art, philosophy and a taste for solitude. It sits on the closing earth branch of the day branch's trine. Traditionally it marks someone set slightly apart, whether by temperament or by calling."},
gNM(){return"The general at the centre of the trine \u2014 authority, command, and the ability to hold a position. It falls on the branch the day branch's group turns around, and lends weight to the pillar it occupies."},
